The build failed because `Intent` isn't in the world's `use` list, so wit-bindgen generates it only at `crate::aap::caps::types::Intent`. The fix is to import it from there.

I did not add the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem authority, and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need `aap:caps/http-client`. The node holds neither, and the target has no WASI adapter. Adding them would also send untrusted message text to a third service before trust is discharged. To get this, add the capabilities to the node's `with` clause in the graph, for example `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>`, or log at the host/runtime boundary where inputs are already visible.

